<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mushikavamsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Mushaka-vamsha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mushikavamsa is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poem composed in the 11th century by the court poet Atula in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>. It recounts the legendary origins of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mushika-dynasty">Mushika dynasty</a> and lists its kings down to the poet's patron. Although its early chronology is unreliable, it is one of the few dynastic chronicles from medieval Kerala and a valuable source for the region's history.</p></div>
